{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:BraidsAndKnots.HeckeCharacterQInteger","@type":"LeanModule","name":"BraidsAndKnots.HeckeCharacterQInteger","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerCanonical"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.qLambert_single_term","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.qLambert_single_term","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/hecke-character-q-integer.lean#L60-L86","doc":"**q-Lambert single-term identity** (the structural root of the\nLi_2^q simple-pole / branch-point analysis, PRs #1657/#1666).\n\n`[n]_q · (q − q⁻¹) · q⁻ⁿ = 1 − q⁻²ⁿ`.\n\nEquivalently `1/[n]_q = (q − q⁻¹)·q⁻ⁿ/(1 − q⁻²ⁿ)`: the inverse\nq-integer is a single geometric (Lambert) kernel in `q⁻²ⁿ`. Summing\nthe geometric series gives the Lambert expansion\n`1/[n]_q = (q − q⁻¹)·Σ_{m≥0} q⁻⁽²ᵐ⁺¹⁾ⁿ`, whose `m`-terms each carry a\nsimple pole at `z = q^{2m+1}` of the Rogers dilogarithm derivative\n`−ln_q(1−z)/z`. The *simple*-pole order is exactly why `z = q₀` is an\nintegrable logarithmic **branch point** (not a pole) of `Li_2^q`, and\nwhy the `+i0` continuation's imaginary part is the `z`-INDEPENDENT\nresidue `π·Res` that cancels in the m_e-normalised ratio\n(`qbeta_li2q_imaginary_quantization.py`, PR #1666 — the reality gate).\n\nProof is `field_simp` + `ring` over `ℝ` (algebraic; the pole/branch\nanalysis is archimedean, real `q > 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.hecke_times_qInteger_five","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.hecke_times_qInteger_five","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/hecke-character-q-integer.lean#L53-L58","doc":"The meson mass ratio identity:\nh·[5]_q = q⁵ − q⁻⁵.\nThis gives the kaon-to-pion character factor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.qInteger_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.qInteger_three","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/hecke-character-q-integer.lean#L45-L51","doc":"[3]_q = q² + 1 + q⁻². ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.qInteger_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.qInteger_two","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/hecke-character-q-integer.lean#L37-L43","doc":"[2]_q = q + q⁻¹. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.hecke_times_qInteger","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.hecke_times_qInteger","kind":"theorem","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/hecke-character-q-integer.lean#L30-L35","doc":"h·[n]_q = qⁿ−q⁻ⁿ: the Hecke parameter times the q-integer\nequals the numerator of the q-integer definition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.qInteger_eq_canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.qInteger_eq_canonical","kind":"theorem","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/hecke-character-q-integer.lean#L25-L28","doc":"**Bridge to the canonical balanced bracket.** The body is already the\ncanonical one; aliasing was refused only because a proof below rewrites with the\nlocal name, so the consolidation is recorded as this (definitional) equation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.qInteger","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.qInteger","kind":"def","line":22,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/hecke-character-q-integer.lean#L22-L23","doc":"The q-integer [n]_q = (qⁿ−q⁻ⁿ)/(q−q⁻¹). ","signatureChunk":0}]}